Z||000000||Rodney||02-18-2000||09:35 PM||||Starting a new power steering post since I can't seem to reply to the current one. <P>I have the aftermarket power steering in my 88 Mera. It is the same as the one you may have seen in IRM's cataloge and Fiero Plus in Canada. It is a Merkuer unit modified to fit.  Pump mounts on the engine just over the water pump.12.5:1 ratio. Nice with my 245-50 Gatorbacks. I was able to buy the second last unit. Another Mera owner bought the last one a few years back. There are no more from the guy that made them.  <P>I also do have a new GM 88 Fiero power steering rack here. When I first contacted the supplier of the rack rebuilding parts they mentioned they had a 88 Fiero power steering rack there. Seems they buy a new rack as they are avalible from the auto makers so they have a reference for rebuild parts. I am still looking for a pump! I have heard there is one in private hands. Maybe someday I'll find it. I doubt this rack ever goes in a Fiero. I will be showing it at Fiero shows. <P>Rodney Dickman ||||reg||1
